{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSWyU17RhcDTvFiWxfpq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- REST controllers use `@RestController` with `@RequestMapping` and `@PostMapping`/@GetMapping` annotations\n- Errors are thrown as `ApiException` subclasses: `ResourceNotFoundException` (404), `ConflictException` (409)\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler` centrally converts exceptions to JSON error envelope with `code`, `message`, and `fields`\n- Controllers return `ResponseEntity` with status for creation, plain domain objects for retrieval\n- Test pattern uses `MockMvc`, `MockMvcRequestBuilders`, and `jsonPath` assertions\n- In-memory repository has `save()`, `findById()`, `existsById()` methods\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` — must add `POST /{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint\n2. `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for confirm operation\n3. `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` — must add error code for invalid state transition (CANCELLED → CONFIRMED)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotent behavior requires checking current status before deciding what to return\n- Must not break existing tests (create, get, list)\n- Error code enum is shared across service; adding a code is necessary but slightly extends scope\n\n**Open questions:**\nWhat error code should represent \"cannot confirm a cancelled shipment\"? The ticket specifies HTTP 409 but doesn't name the code. Looking at existing patterns (SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS), I'll add SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION to make error cases clear to clients.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This codes the semantic error of attempting to confirm a shipment in CANCELLED status.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method:\n   - Retrieve shipment by ID; if not found, throw `ResourceNotFoundException` (404)\n   - If shipment status is `CREATED`, update it to `CONFIRMED`, save, and return the updated shipment\n   - If shipment status is `CONFIRMED`, return it unchanged (idempotent success)\n   - If shipment status is `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION` (409)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` — POST confirm on CREATED, expect 200 with CONFIRMED status\n   - `is idempotent for already confirmed shipment` — POST confirm twice on CREATED, expect both to succeed with 200\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment` — write CANCELLED shipment to repo, POST confirm, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION\n   - `reports unknown shipment on confirm attempt` — POST confirm to non-existent ID, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using existing error code like `VALIDATION_FAILED` or reusing `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` — rejected because neither is semantically accurate. The shipment exists; the issue is a disallowed state transition. Adding a specific error code makes the API contract clearer for clients.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Path | Read | Write | Response |\n|------|-------|------|------|-------|----------|\n| Confirm CREATED | `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm` | Happy | findById(S-1) → CREATED | save(S-1 with CONFIRMED) | 200 + updated shipment |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED | `POST /shipments/S-2/confirm` (called twice) | Idempotent | findById(S-2) → CONFIRMED | (none) | 200 + unchanged shipment |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | `POST /shipments/S-3/confirm` | Error | findById(S-3) → CANCELLED | (none) | 409 ConflictException + SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION |\n| Confirm missing | `POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm` | Error | findById() → null | (none) | 404 ResourceNotFoundException + SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `confirmCreatedShipment` — Exercises the main happy path: CREATED → CONFIRMED transition, persistence, and response correctness\n2. `confirmIsIdempotent` — Verifies repeated calls on CONFIRMED shipment succeed without side effects, satisfying operations retry requirement\n3. `rejectConfirmingCancelledShipment` — Validates 409 response and correct error code for invalid state transition\n4. `reportUnknownShipmentOnConfirm` — Validates 404 response and error code consistency with GET by ID\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":735,"cache_read_input_tokens":14636,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":735},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35883cf2-89bc-40cc-bab0-d47546c07d6d","uuid":"6485915a-35ee-455f-9a64-ed63916a8803","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:23:59.122Z","request_id":"req_011CfSWyTd3hNT6sQ3fazK1W"}
